# Baseline binary assets are distributed through the registry, not this Git tree.
#
# Tracked unified diffs under patches/ are DATA, not source: source-patches.mjs
# feeds them to `git apply -p1` inside a scratch directory, and `git apply`
# matches context lines byte-for-byte. The upstream tarballs these diffs target
# use LF, while `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this
# machine has) rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout — so a clean clone
# produces CRLF diffs whose context can never match, and the whole repack
# pipeline dies with "patch does not apply".
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths, so the working
# copy is byte-identical to the blob regardless of core.autocrlf. Keep the
# spelling as `-text` (not `text eol=lf`): both are correct, but a second,
# differently-spelled rule for the same paths makes future merges conflict
# instead of agreeing.
patches/**/*.diff -text
